WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.963
Wrist cameras provide an action-centric view,

00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:05.407
but they are hard to collect at scale.

00:00:05.857 --> 00:00:08.898
Egocentric video is much easier to scale.

00:00:09.457 --> 00:00:14.503
We introduce Ego2Wrist: bootstrapping wrist-view synthesis from egocentric video.

00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:20.370
A video diffusion model denoises both wrist views right next to the head view,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.971
so we can synthesize wrist views for any in-the-wild video.

00:00:24.421 --> 00:00:26.948
How do we know if the in-the-wild samples are good?

00:00:27.621 --> 00:00:31.470
We introduce HCC: hand-centric cross-view consistency.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.905
It checks that the wrist view agrees with the head view around the hand.

00:00:34.905 --> 00:00:36.789
No wrist ground truth needed.

00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:40.435
So the model teaches itself:

00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:43.289
synthesize wrist views for in-the-wild video,

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:44.670
keep the top 30%,

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.220
train on them, and repeat.

00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:50.300
Every round lowers the error further,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.768
without collecting a single new wrist video.

00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:56.606
Versus WorldWander, the error drops by 28%.

00:00:59.056 --> 00:01:02.041
Paper, code, and weights are all online.
